# 9. SAFE PYTHON PROJECT

We can create a visible Tkinter application.

The application will:

- Display a text box
- Capture key events only in that window
- Display the event
- Write events to a local lab log
- Allow the user to stop logging
- Not run in the background
- Not capture other applications

---

# 10. SAFE KEY EVENT LOGGER

```python
import tkinter as tk
from datetime import datetime
from pathlib import Path

LOG_FILE = Path("lab_key_events.txt")


def log_key(event):
    timestamp = datetime.now().isoformat(timespec="seconds")

    # Record only the key name, not the text content.
    entry = f"{timestamp} | key={event.keysym}\n"

    with LOG_FILE.open("a", encoding="utf-8") as file:
        file.write(entry)

    status_var.set(f"Last key event: {event.keysym}")


def stop_logging():
    text_box.unbind("<KeyPress>")
    status_var.set("Logging stopped.")


root = tk.Tk()
root.title("Ethical Key Event Logger - Lab")
root.geometry("650x350")

warning = tk.Label(
    root,
    text="LAB ONLY — Logs keyboard events only inside this window.",
    font=("Arial", 11, "bold")
)
warning.pack(pady=10)

text_box = tk.Text(root, height=10, width=70)
text_box.pack(padx=10, pady=10)

status_var = tk.StringVar(value="Logging active.")
status = tk.Label(root, textvariable=status_var)
status.pack(pady=5)

stop_button = tk.Button(
    root,
    text="Stop Logging",
    command=stop_logging
)
stop_button.pack(pady=10)

text_box.bind("<KeyPress>", log_key)

root.mainloop()
```

