# 15. EVENT-DRIVEN PROGRAMMING

The important Python concept here is:

> **The program waits for an event and executes a function when that event occurs.**

Example:

```python
text_box.bind("<KeyPress>", log_key)
```

Conceptually:

```text
KeyPress
   ↓
log_key()
   ↓
Process event
```

