# 31. DEFENSIVE CONTROLS

Organizations can reduce keylogger risk using:

### Endpoint protection

EDR/antimalware can detect suspicious programs.

### Application control

Allow only approved software.

### Least privilege

Reduce what malicious programs can access.

### MFA

Even if a password is captured, additional authentication factors can reduce account compromise.

### Password managers

Reduce exposure to manual password entry in some workflows.

### Network monitoring

Detect suspicious outbound communication.

### Patching

Reduce initial compromise opportunities.

---

# 32. WHY MFA HELPS

Suppose a keylogger captures:

```text
Username
Password
```

With strong MFA:

```text
Username
Password
+
Additional factor
```

The attacker may still be unable to authenticate.

However:

> MFA does not make keyloggers harmless.

They can still capture other sensitive information and may target authentication flows differently.

